      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_05cd29944d068c309d1f203b0a6c93dff1a034a521e9e6990d8a4641d70dee91",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Source fact: reordering the corrected building block and applying Q-duality gives a w-reflection; applying the GL(3) functional equation and P-duality gives an s-reflection. Signed-divisor character variants are assembled into finite vectors on which meromorphic matrices implement both transformations. Interpretation: the vector state absorbs congruence and bad-prime changes, closing both summation orders under controlled matrix transitions even though no scalar component is invariant. This is an input to continuation, not continuation itself: matrix entries may add auxiliary poles or zeros and genuine poles are not yet classified.",
