    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_6e3e7a09cf927b43b92f35b95c65faae8dc6d178e3805f7a50a77d35a6784e35",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Source fact: for degrees one through three the corrected double Dirichlet series has a finite functional-equation group, uniquely determined correction factors, and reflected convergence regions whose convex hull gives full continuation; the paper separately proves cubic moment results. From degree four, the group is infinite and uniqueness fails, while a barrier of essential singularities is presented as an apparent correspondence. Interpretation: finiteness closes both the local correction system and this reflection-plus-convexity continuation method, making the cubic case the last completely understood case of that method. The higher-degree continuation obstruction is expected, not proved equivalent to infinitude or nonuniqueness.",
