    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_fc7301f489c273a2a5e154b309b72e80d748cc918837035ffaa65691054d0250",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Source fact: the square-constrained residue has an Euler product from which the source extracts one-variable zeta factors ζ(2s_i) and pairwise factors ζ(s_i+s_j); the remaining factor R is holomorphic slightly left of the central point and its central local-factor comparison gives a_m. Interpretation: standard singular factors are peeled from regular prime-local density, exposing the conjectural arithmetic constant in the residue. This factorization does not generate the reflected poles or a continuation neighborhood, so it cannot alone yield the family moment asymptotic.",
