    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_4b52410b332acf7b69534f4fe2fd691de0d825b96b0b1b1a2c35a983d313a314",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For the cubic construction, finite closure links three otherwise separate tasks. The duality and interchange constraints uniquely determine the imprimitive correction polynomials through GL(3); those corrections allow congruence and bad-prime character variants to be packaged into a finite vector closed under the s- and w-reflections; the resulting finite dihedral action moves overlapping pole-cleared tube domains whose successive convex hulls fill C^2. At degree four the source records both loss of uniqueness and an infinite functional-equation group, and the reflected absolute-convergence region no longer reaches the central point, identifying a concrete obstruction to this correction-plus-reflection continuation method.",
