    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c8a9311225c68320b3e55681c1c4350a363ae6de137cdbb7ec68d72c64523ae4",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The proof deliberately changes arithmetic representations before returning to the target family. Correction polynomials and finite character vectors first create an all-integer double Dirichlet series closed under two functional equations; reflected tube convexity continues a pole-cleared version, and functional-equation paths then supply strip bounds and eliminate artificial bad-prime pole candidates. Two inclusion-exclusion layers, backed by uniform modulus bounds, remove nontrivial square factors and recombine signs, congruence classes, and the prime-2 factor to recover the fundamental-discriminant series. Only after this transfer does the triangular Mellin kernel shift the contour and turn the seventh-order pole into the weighted cubic-moment polynomial.",
